{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1530081-gods-innately-commanding-lesser-gods-2e","id":1530081,"title":"Gods innately commanding lesser gods? (2E)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-02-06T02:23:51-08:00","id":1530081,"title":"Gods innately commanding lesser gods? (2E)","content":"Someone was asking a question on the Exalted reddit about how to gives gods the ability to bind other gods. It jogged my memory but now I don't know if I just made it up.<br /> <br /> Does anyone recall an element of the lore/mechanics from 2E where any god could innately give orders to any god that was of a lower essence rating than them? And what book might it have been in? I was thinking the Yu-Shan compass one or Rolls of Glorious Divinity but not having any luck.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4612-solar-lantern","name":"Solar Lantern","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4612_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"77"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-06T07:40:21-08:00","id":1530092,"title":"","content":"Exalted Second Edition core rulebook, p. 295, under Willpower and Health Levels. Roll of Glorious Divinity: Gods and Elementals, p. 169, elaborates on this (and how to resist it) and gives it the name of the Mandate of Subordination.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-06T08:33:19-08:00","id":1530095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1530081-gods-innately-commanding-lesser-gods-2e?p=1530092#post1530092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exalted Second Edition core rulebook, p. 295, under Willpower and Health Levels. Roll of Glorious Divinity: Gods and Elementals, p. 169, elaborates on this (and how to resist it) and gives it the name of the Mandate of Subordination.</div> </div> </div> </div>Excellent, thank you <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4612-solar-lantern","name":"Solar Lantern","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4612_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"77"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-12T08:56:29-08:00","id":1530646,"title":"","content":"I think Mandate of Subordination may have been dropped from the current repertoire of gods, possibly because it makes their hierarchy too limited; it affords those on top too much of an effortless way to ensure compliance, and those below too little room for scheming. That's an issue with the kind of society they seem to want spirits to have.<br /> <br /> Under the current system, I think a god who wants a tighter grip on subordinate gods needs to enlist the aid of sorcerers or gods whose Charms would be inclined to that, if for no other reason than it ties them into a deeper network of obligation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-16T18:05:14-08:00","id":1531014,"title":"","content":"I always thought the way for a lesser god to defy Mandate of Subordination was with a perfect mental dodge or something. That is to say, any sufficiently heroic/tenacious/plot-important god just kind of develops one the vague way all spirits seem to in order to rise to the challenge of saying &quot;no&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26460-organ-boy","name":"Organ Boy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-16T19:20:05-08:00","id":1531016,"title":"","content":"Any god can defy the Mandate of Subordination by paying Willpower equal to the difference in Essence to their superior, which protects them from repeated attempts for the rest of the scene. A perfect mental dodge will also work, but remember that aside from rare and expensive All-Encompassing variant Charms, all divine Charms have some kind of added limitation related to the god's purview or nature.<br /> <br /> And yes, this is from Second Edition, I don't think Third Edition has the Mandate of Subordination in the first place. Probably a wise choice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":522,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","user":"Stupid Loserman","date":". 02-16-2024, 10:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}